WEBVTT

00:01.544 --> 00:04.590
<i>♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.634 --> 00:07.640
<i>♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪</i>

00:07.767 --> 00:11.358
<i>♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.444 --> 00:14.365
<i>♪ on which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.451 --> 00:17.790
<i>♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:17.876 --> 00:21.340
<i>♪ lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.426 --> 00:22.885
<i>♪ all the things that make us ♪</i>

00:22.970 --> 00:24.139
<i>♪ laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.266 --> 00:30.154
<i>♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:34.916 --> 00:36.126
Good morning, family.

00:36.212 --> 00:38.381
Now, as you all know,
since four minutes ago,

00:38.467 --> 00:40.011
When I heard it on the radio,

00:40.138 --> 00:41.847
It has been my lifelong dream

00:41.934 --> 00:44.563
To compete in the st. Philip's
greasy pole contest,

00:44.607 --> 00:47.862
Where shirtless men try
to climb across a greasy pole.

00:47.948 --> 00:49.033
Come on, chris, let's go.

00:49.160 --> 00:50.787
Now, hold on, peter,
you promised

00:50.914 --> 00:52.332
You'd run errands with me today.

00:52.417 --> 00:55.215
You can't just bail 'cause
you heard of some fun new thing.

00:55.342 --> 00:58.639
Lois, we both know I'm going to
the whatever-I-just-said thing.

00:58.725 --> 00:59.474
Meg will fill in for me.

00:59.643 --> 01:00.979
Ugh, fine.

01:01.106 --> 01:03.151
All right, now, if you're
gonna be filling in for me,

01:03.194 --> 01:05.197
You need to complete
the online course.

01:06.326 --> 01:08.956
<i>Congratulations on being picked
to fill in for me</i>

01:09.041 --> 01:10.711
<i>While I have a horse-around day.</i>

01:10.796 --> 01:13.760
<i> Now, let's talk dos and don'ts
around the workplace.</i>

01:14.973 --> 01:16.641
<i> Okay, let's see what
you've learned.</i>

01:16.768 --> 01:19.733
<i>Describe the difference between
a tunic and a shawl</i>

01:19.860 --> 01:21.570
<i> In as much detail as possible.</i>

01:21.655 --> 01:22.698
Ugh.

01:23.493 --> 01:24.952
<i> Congratulations on being
picked...</i>

01:25.080 --> 01:26.959
Every year there's some hotshot
who thinks

01:27.086 --> 01:29.255
They don't gotta watch
the video.

01:34.604 --> 01:36.941
Oh, no, I left my phone
in the car.

01:37.068 --> 01:38.905
Oh, weird. I forgot mine, too.

01:38.990 --> 01:40.241
Should I run back and grab them?

01:40.326 --> 01:42.246
-Oh, we don't need 'em.
-No, we do not.

01:42.289 --> 01:45.295
I for one welcome
the lost art of conversation,

01:45.381 --> 01:47.717
Of which we are both ninjas,
my friend.

01:47.844 --> 01:49.846
Absolutely.

01:53.191 --> 01:54.734
<i>♪ bah dah buh buh ba ♪</i>

01:54.861 --> 01:57.909
<i>♪ bah dah buh buh da dah! ♪</i>

01:58.036 --> 01:59.328
So, how you doing, man?

01:59.498 --> 02:02.377
All good. All good in the hood.

02:02.462 --> 02:04.133
Anything new? What's new?

02:04.218 --> 02:06.638
Same old, same old.
Life good? Family good?

02:06.765 --> 02:07.933
Yep, living the dream.

02:08.019 --> 02:11.066
D-r-e-a-m. No complaints.

02:11.193 --> 02:12.528
Zero complaints.

02:12.613 --> 02:15.025
Dylan, right? Your son. He good?

02:15.119 --> 02:16.580
Most def.

02:17.792 --> 02:19.545
Most def.

02:20.382 --> 02:21.967
[cell phone alerts chiming]

02:22.094 --> 02:24.390
-Breaking news.
-I can't believe this.

02:24.476 --> 02:26.687
I have a samsung, so my alert
hasn't come in yet.

02:26.773 --> 02:29.027
It's nice not being glued
to our phones

02:29.112 --> 02:30.363
Like these sheeple, huh?

02:30.448 --> 02:31.366
[samsung phone chimes]

02:31.451 --> 02:33.620
[man] there it is. Oh, my god.

02:33.748 --> 02:35.919
Slaves to the screen.

02:44.400 --> 02:46.025
Are we almost done?

02:46.152 --> 02:47.823
I need to find
stewie's rash cream,

02:47.908 --> 02:50.036
But if you're not having fun,
go get a squeeze

02:50.163 --> 02:51.665
From the blood pressure machine.

02:51.750 --> 02:53.754
That always perks me up.

02:54.967 --> 02:57.471
[phone chiming]

02:57.598 --> 02:59.893
<i> Meg, oh, my god,
it's crazy here.</i>

03:00.021 --> 03:02.483
<i> Dad fell off the pole
and landed on his head,</i>

03:02.610 --> 03:04.446
<i>And one of his eyes popped out.</i>

03:04.614 --> 03:06.577
<i> We picked it up
and jammed it back in,</i>

03:06.745 --> 03:09.667
<i> But the pupil was
on the other side.</i>

03:09.794 --> 03:11.463
<i> I'm okay.
Just got a little headache.</i>

03:11.548 --> 03:14.052
<i> Also, dad gave me
a hard lemonade.</i>

03:14.138 --> 03:15.974
<i> He's pretty out of it.</i>

03:16.644 --> 03:19.149
Total shocker,
chris and dad are having

03:19.234 --> 03:20.359
A very fun day.

03:20.487 --> 03:22.239
They're not the only ones, huh?

03:22.366 --> 03:24.620
Oh, I also need to return
this loofah.

03:24.706 --> 03:26.666
I mean, who was I kidding?
I'm a dial bar

03:26.710 --> 03:29.089
-Smeared right on the skin gal.
-Of course.

03:29.250 --> 03:31.972
Let me show you
to the returns section.

03:32.099 --> 03:34.268
[explosion]

03:34.355 --> 03:37.443
<i>[mort]
the prestige.</i>

03:40.077 --> 03:43.374
Well, I guess janet
forgave robert for jamaica.

03:43.418 --> 03:45.504
-What are you talking about?
-The wedding's back on.

03:45.632 --> 03:48.804
And janet officially has
no backbone.

03:48.931 --> 03:50.058
What are you doing?

03:50.143 --> 03:51.561
Um, eating a sandwich.

03:51.729 --> 03:54.359
Brian griffin,
I ordered ramen for us.

03:54.444 --> 03:55.737
We planned this last night.

03:55.864 --> 03:58.077
We did?
I don't-- I don't remember.

03:58.162 --> 03:59.747
You were too drunk to remember?

03:59.874 --> 04:01.293
I've been dying
to try this place.

04:01.420 --> 04:02.755
You said we could
do it together.

04:02.841 --> 04:04.342
-Stewie, it's not--
-[knock on door]

04:05.973 --> 04:08.143
Uh, ramen for stewie and brian?

04:08.228 --> 04:10.064
Apparently it's just for stewie.

04:10.150 --> 04:12.194
-Everything okay?
-No, it's not!

04:12.322 --> 04:14.450
[sobbing]

04:14.535 --> 04:15.871
Stewie, what the hell was that?

04:15.998 --> 04:17.206
What happened to us?

04:17.292 --> 04:18.668
I thought we were best friends.

04:18.755 --> 04:20.088
We have nothing to say
at brunch,

04:20.174 --> 04:22.345
We don't listen to each other,
we forget plans we made.

04:22.472 --> 04:24.683
By the way, the
"we" in all this is you.

04:24.769 --> 04:26.729
Don't be dramatic,
stewie, we're fine.

04:26.857 --> 04:29.487
No, we're not.
Best friends talk about stuff.

04:29.614 --> 04:31.700
I-I don't--
what do you want me to do?

04:31.786 --> 04:34.333
If you're really asking,
I saw a therapist

04:34.418 --> 04:35.752
<i>On the today show talking about</i>

04:35.879 --> 04:38.216
The emergence of
friendship therapy.

04:38.259 --> 04:39.344
I think it could help us.

04:39.471 --> 04:41.892
-No.
-[crying]

04:41.936 --> 04:44.398
-[sighs] fine.
-Oh, brian, this is great.

04:44.525 --> 04:46.320
It'll give us
the fresh start we need.

04:46.489 --> 04:48.658
Like when tom brady
moved to tampa bay.

04:48.744 --> 04:52.376
All right!
Now I get to cheat in shorts.

04:52.504 --> 04:55.718
I'm peyton manning,
and I approve this message.

05:00.230 --> 05:04.195
So, yeah, this is how I reload
my purse with mom stuff.

05:04.323 --> 05:07.705
-It's very important
to always be prepared.
-Didn't ask.

05:07.832 --> 05:09.876
Travel-size lotion,
hand sanitizer,

05:09.962 --> 05:12.633
Tic tacs, so I can
skip brushing my teeth.

05:12.719 --> 05:14.304
Dawg, you still gotta brush.

05:14.348 --> 05:16.309
Oh, and mom hack 68:

05:16.394 --> 05:18.523
Buy the $2.00
plastic rain bonnet.

05:18.609 --> 05:22.406
They're made at the same factory
that makes the $9.00 ones.

05:22.493 --> 05:25.999
Don't ask me how I know.

05:27.087 --> 05:29.549
Oh, meg, don't look for a sec.

05:30.387 --> 05:32.808
Okay, it's safe.

05:33.896 --> 05:37.027
Our treat for an epic
errands day.

05:37.154 --> 05:39.156
Amazing.

05:39.326 --> 05:41.871
Big surprise, I didn't win.

05:41.957 --> 05:43.626
Didn't win what?

05:47.470 --> 05:50.475
Oh, my god, meg, I won!

05:51.940 --> 05:54.569
You're kidding.
Mom, this is amazing.

05:54.655 --> 05:56.323
Ah! I know, I can't believe it.

05:56.409 --> 05:59.706
It's even more exciting than
the creation of broccolini.

05:59.791 --> 06:01.587
What is this new plant?

06:01.714 --> 06:03.006
Let me ask you a question.

06:03.049 --> 06:05.012
-Do you like broccoli?
-Not really.

06:05.139 --> 06:09.940
Well, I think I just figured out
a way to make it harder to eat.

06:13.325 --> 06:15.494
I can't believe
you won ten grand.

06:15.623 --> 06:17.959
I know. I wonder how soon
I can get that

06:18.045 --> 06:20.174
House water filtration system
installed.

06:20.259 --> 06:21.928
A couple weeks? A month?

06:22.013 --> 06:24.266
-What is wrong with you?
-Wh-what do you mean?

06:24.352 --> 06:26.773
You win a boatload of money,
and your first thought is

06:26.901 --> 06:28.526
A water filtration system?!

06:28.612 --> 06:31.115
How do you not
blow your brains out?

06:31.243 --> 06:33.206
Oh, these systems are very cool.

06:33.291 --> 06:35.502
No, they're not! They're boring.

06:35.630 --> 06:37.632
<i>Everything you do is boring.</i>

06:37.759 --> 06:39.805
That's why we all want
to hang out with dad.

06:39.890 --> 06:41.642
Imagine what he'd do
with ten grand.

06:41.812 --> 06:44.858
Something super stupid
and selfish and awesome,

06:44.987 --> 06:46.028
That's what.

06:50.123 --> 06:53.839
-Dad's not the only
fun one, you know.
-Uh-huh?

06:53.882 --> 06:56.135
Oh, you don't believe me?
Okay, okay.

06:56.221 --> 06:58.642
Well, what if--
what if we use the money

06:58.769 --> 07:00.731
For something fun? For just us.

07:00.816 --> 07:03.446
-Like what?
-Like going on a top-secret

07:03.531 --> 07:05.659
-Mother/daughter trip.
-Really?

07:05.786 --> 07:07.914
Mom, that would be amazing.

07:08.042 --> 07:10.630
Great. Now let's keep
this same energy

07:10.749 --> 07:13.344
While we take a quick detour
for my mammogram.

07:13.472 --> 07:15.683
Whoo-hoo! Girls' trip!

07:15.810 --> 07:16.937
How's it looking in there?

07:17.023 --> 07:19.568
<i>Well, it's probably nothing.</i>

07:19.695 --> 07:22.074
[weakly]
ooh, girls' trip.

07:27.296 --> 07:29.551
<i> [man over p.A.] final call
for vacation airlines flight</i>

07:29.720 --> 07:31.096
<i> To vacation destination.</i>

07:31.224 --> 07:33.351
I can't believe we're
going on a secret trip.

07:33.478 --> 07:36.025
This is so cool.
What did you tell dad?

07:36.152 --> 07:37.987
Oh, pfft, he won't even know
we're gone.

07:38.116 --> 07:39.783
I got him
his favorite babysitter.

07:39.868 --> 07:42.749
Lois says we're allowed
to stay up past 9:00.

07:42.835 --> 07:44.420
The note says 9:00.

07:44.548 --> 07:45.714
Not if it's special.

07:45.800 --> 07:47.302
<i>And we're allowed
to watch beetlejuice.</i>

07:47.388 --> 07:50.894
<i>The note specifically says
"no beetlejuice."</i>

07:52.567 --> 07:53.735
<i>I'm allowed to watch coco,</i>

07:53.821 --> 07:56.324
And it's basically
the same thing.

08:00.796 --> 08:03.633
I'm dr. Wagner.
Please take a seat.

08:03.720 --> 08:05.012
This is a test, right?

08:05.097 --> 08:07.852
You're free to sit
anywhere you like.

08:09.274 --> 08:10.775
Yeah? This right?

08:10.861 --> 08:13.158
There's no right or wrong.

08:16.041 --> 08:18.211
Aha, you lost.
You sat too quick.

08:18.338 --> 08:20.257
Are you uncomfortable
that brian had the confidence

08:20.384 --> 08:21.803
-To choose a seat?
-Yes!

08:21.889 --> 08:23.181
Brian one, stewie zero.

08:23.308 --> 08:25.688
Actually, brian,
this isn't a contest.

08:25.774 --> 08:27.191
Yes. One to one.

08:27.276 --> 08:28.402
Stewie, please sit.

08:28.488 --> 08:29.696
I may just stand.

08:29.782 --> 08:31.744
Oh, indecisive. Two to one.

08:31.830 --> 08:34.668
Doc's going pen to pad,
and you gotta think

08:34.753 --> 08:37.090
Stewie just evened up the score.

08:43.859 --> 08:46.655
It does look like we have
an ocean-view suite available

08:46.825 --> 08:49.202
For an extra $500
if you are interested.

08:49.289 --> 08:52.002
You know what, yes,
we'll take it.

08:52.087 --> 08:54.257
The snapple babes are
living it up.

08:54.342 --> 08:55.509
Very good.

08:55.637 --> 08:57.098
So the room isn't quite ready.

08:57.183 --> 08:58.810
Would you like to inconveniently

08:58.937 --> 08:59.980
Grab your swimsuits
from your luggage

09:00.065 --> 09:01.232
And use the pool while you wait?

09:01.401 --> 09:04.365
Oh, that's okay,
we'll just buy new bathing suits

09:04.492 --> 09:06.203
At the lobby store.

09:06.247 --> 09:07.497
[all gasp]

09:07.583 --> 09:09.295
Snapple babes?

09:09.422 --> 09:10.672
And for our survey,

09:10.758 --> 09:11.967
How'd you hear about the resort?

09:12.136 --> 09:14.933
That rich lady from the news
was murdered here.

09:15.019 --> 09:17.481
Yep, that is what
most people say.

09:20.573 --> 09:22.159
Hey, stewie,
what are you watching?

09:22.286 --> 09:25.458
<i>-Uh, uh, the gilded age.
-Seriously?!</i>

09:25.502 --> 09:26.836
I couldn't wait, I'm sorry.

09:26.963 --> 09:28.257
I'll watch it again
with you tonight.

09:28.385 --> 09:29.885
Oh, and have you stare at me
right before

09:30.013 --> 09:31.681
Something big happens? No way.

09:31.809 --> 09:32.975
You know what,
you know what, good.

09:33.062 --> 09:34.314
I'll watch shows on my own, too.

09:34.441 --> 09:36.903
I can finally watch something
after 7:00 p.M.

09:37.030 --> 09:40.161
Dr. Wagner would want us to play
big problem, small problem.

09:40.288 --> 09:43.168
A big problem is sometimes
a hospital problem.

09:43.254 --> 09:44.922
A small problem is
something like

09:44.966 --> 09:46.176
Your friend watches a show--

09:46.345 --> 09:48.347
I'm not listening to this crap.
This is stupid.

09:48.474 --> 09:50.352
You feel like this is stupid?

09:50.479 --> 09:53.318
Dr. Wagner says to use
"I feel" statements.

09:53.404 --> 09:56.032
<i>I feel like you are
making up rules--</i>

09:56.118 --> 09:57.661
Oh, stewie's got the ipad.

09:57.746 --> 09:59.750
Stewie, daddy's just gonna
take the ipad

09:59.878 --> 10:01.463
Into the bathroom, okay?

10:01.590 --> 10:03.843
He took my etch a sketch.

10:03.970 --> 10:07.519
[peter]
siri, show me "busty latinas."

10:07.605 --> 10:10.903
<i> Busty latinas.</i>

10:10.988 --> 10:13.868
Can somebody reset the wi-fi?

10:19.592 --> 10:21.178
-Have you decided?
-Yes.

10:21.263 --> 10:24.394
We'd like two lava flows
in hollowed-out pineapples,

10:24.522 --> 10:27.735
And sweet potato fries
in a hollowed-out coconut.

10:27.862 --> 10:29.154
Any food or drink you bring us

10:29.240 --> 10:31.410
Should be inside
a hollow fruit.

10:31.538 --> 10:34.292
Excuse me, my son and I
couldn't help but notice

10:34.378 --> 10:37.592
You ordered all your food
in hollowed-out fruit.

10:37.678 --> 10:39.012
You must be very rich.

10:39.181 --> 10:41.016
Oh, thanks for noticing.

10:41.186 --> 10:42.145
So what are your names?

10:42.231 --> 10:44.484
You can call us
the snapple babes.

10:44.570 --> 10:46.990
[chuckles] yeah, we're famous.

10:47.075 --> 10:48.662
Well, maybe you can tell us

10:48.789 --> 10:49.998
All about it over dinner.

10:50.083 --> 10:52.003
Shall we say one of
the three overpriced

10:52.088 --> 10:53.505
Hotel restaurants at 8:00?

10:53.591 --> 10:56.973
-[chuckles] we shall.
-See you then.

11:04.577 --> 11:06.287
I forgot these are prescription,

11:06.456 --> 11:09.629
But those are two
smokin'-hot blobs.

11:14.142 --> 11:16.562
So, last session
I asked you each

11:16.606 --> 11:19.109
To write a love song
to your friendship.

11:19.236 --> 11:21.032
Let's start with brian.

11:21.159 --> 11:22.994
Whatever. [clears throat]

11:23.081 --> 11:24.498
<i>♪ stewie, stewie ♪</i>

11:24.583 --> 11:26.370
<i>♪ oh, yeah ♪</i>

11:26.422 --> 11:27.631
<i>♪ awesome guy. ♪</i>

11:27.716 --> 11:29.844
What the hell was that?
You couldn't be bothered

11:29.931 --> 11:31.933
To spend five minutes
preparing something?

11:32.060 --> 11:34.356
Like it matters.
This is so stupid.

11:34.441 --> 11:35.233
You're stupid!

11:35.276 --> 11:36.444
[grunting, straining]

11:36.488 --> 11:37.655
Guys, please.

11:37.740 --> 11:39.452
Admit you exaggerate
your accent.

11:39.538 --> 11:43.168
Admit you wear shirts from
museums you've never been to.

11:43.922 --> 11:45.968
Enough!

11:46.595 --> 11:48.013
This is ridiculous.

11:48.100 --> 11:49.642
Your relationship is toxic.

11:49.769 --> 11:51.732
You're not married,
you're not blood relatives.

11:51.860 --> 11:53.318
Why continue?

11:53.446 --> 11:55.073
[inhales deeply]

11:55.159 --> 11:57.621
In my entire career,

11:57.749 --> 12:01.380
I have never given this advice,
but it is my opinion

12:01.466 --> 12:04.805
That you should end
this friendship.

12:04.891 --> 12:07.269
-Fine by me.
-Makes my life easier.

12:07.397 --> 12:08.981
Also, your insurance card
didn't go through,

12:09.150 --> 12:10.695
And when I looked again
I realized

12:10.822 --> 12:12.156
It was a robek's juice card.

12:12.241 --> 12:13.994
You went to suny albany.

12:14.079 --> 12:15.790
You'll take it and like it.

12:18.590 --> 12:21.178
Okay, this is
a bartering culture,

12:21.263 --> 12:23.309
So we have to haggle over
an amount of money

12:23.436 --> 12:26.191
We wouldn't even pick up
if we dropped it on the ground.

12:28.573 --> 12:30.785
[both gasp, yelp]

12:30.912 --> 12:32.623
[both grunting]

12:32.750 --> 12:35.463
[tires squealing]

12:35.591 --> 12:37.426
[meg]
mom, what are they gonna do
with us?

12:37.554 --> 12:39.138
[lois]
if you let my daughter go,

12:39.224 --> 12:40.809
You can do whatever you want
to me.

12:40.895 --> 12:44.569
In the following order:
You, you, blond-arm-hair guy,

12:44.654 --> 12:46.489
You two,
maybe a quick lunch and shower,

12:46.575 --> 12:48.787
Then blond-arm-hair guy again
if he's into it.

12:53.551 --> 12:55.554
♪ ♪

13:01.236 --> 13:02.946
[gasps]
you two?

13:03.033 --> 13:04.658
Where are we?

13:09.047 --> 13:10.548
It's a co-kidnapping space.

13:10.675 --> 13:12.094
It used to be a wework.

13:12.180 --> 13:14.057
Oh, I saw that documentary.
Meh.

13:14.100 --> 13:15.519
Sorry to interrupt.

13:15.605 --> 13:17.523
Is there, like, a trick
to the keurig machine?

13:17.609 --> 13:19.905
Hey, man. Yeah,
it's probably just out of water.

13:22.789 --> 13:24.332
God, there's nothing in here.

13:24.459 --> 13:25.836
Where's the money?

13:25.880 --> 13:27.799
Uh, I'd look in the lobby store.

13:27.926 --> 13:30.262
Ah, guilty as charged. [laughs]

13:30.348 --> 13:32.435
No, but they do have fun stuff
in there.

13:32.521 --> 13:35.192
Shut up! The real money will
be the ransom, anyways.

13:35.277 --> 13:37.280
We've never captured
a beverage heiress before.

13:37.409 --> 13:39.619
What?! Who do you think we are?

13:39.705 --> 13:42.000
We know
you're the snapple family.

13:42.127 --> 13:43.294
[laughing]
oh, no.

13:43.381 --> 13:45.592
This is a big misunderstanding.

13:45.678 --> 13:49.268
We just won a snapple contest,
then spent all the money.

13:49.353 --> 13:50.897
[scoffs]
you're worthless!

13:50.983 --> 13:52.358
[mechanical whirring]

13:52.445 --> 13:54.906
<i>[kidnapper]
it was the water.</i>

13:55.034 --> 13:57.371
[string instruments playing]

13:57.498 --> 14:00.336
And do you, janet, take robert
to be your husband?

14:00.464 --> 14:01.757
I do.

14:01.884 --> 14:03.178
...Forgive you about jamaica.

14:03.305 --> 14:05.182
[chuckles softly]
am I right?

14:09.361 --> 14:11.197
Brian, what are you doing here?

14:11.324 --> 14:12.700
I should ask you that.

14:12.786 --> 14:14.622
Can't believe you came,
knowing I'd be here.

14:14.707 --> 14:17.378
Well, I'm not gonna punish janet
for what happened between us.

14:17.506 --> 14:19.341
Okay,
but just keep your distance.

14:19.426 --> 14:21.263
Fine, I get from the bar

14:21.349 --> 14:23.644
To the bridesmaid
having a terse, ugly argument

14:23.771 --> 14:24.813
With her boyfriend.

14:24.941 --> 14:26.943
Okay, and I get from her

14:27.028 --> 14:31.246
To the bald uncle looking around
before telling a racist joke.

14:32.249 --> 14:33.584
So, how long we thinking

14:33.754 --> 14:35.714
Until stewie makes
this whole event about him?

14:35.800 --> 14:38.721
Ten minutes? Shall we put
a little cashish on it?

14:38.807 --> 14:40.936
I just asked you
to pass the butter.

14:41.021 --> 14:42.898
I don't know who stewie is.

14:42.942 --> 14:44.735
Do yourself a favor,
keep it that way.

14:44.863 --> 14:47.535
I think we're supposed to sit
at the tables we were assigned.

14:47.662 --> 14:50.292
Yeah, no, they said
I could kind of be a roamer.

14:52.090 --> 14:53.633
[sniffs]
smells like butt.

14:53.760 --> 14:55.555
Let me guess.
Brian was just here?

14:55.640 --> 14:57.934
-Who's brian?
-I think that's the dog guy.

14:58.062 --> 15:00.984
I thought this table was just
supposed to be cornell people.

15:06.041 --> 15:08.586
Oh, my god.
Mom, we're gonna die.

15:12.431 --> 15:13.891
Oh, no, we're not.

15:14.018 --> 15:15.519
I have a plan.

15:15.647 --> 15:17.484
Uh, hey, guys,
you know, if you're hungry,

15:17.653 --> 15:19.821
I have a half a granola bar
in my purse.

15:19.908 --> 15:22.620
This purse is useless,
just like you!

15:23.500 --> 15:24.709
Huh. The good people

15:24.795 --> 15:27.173
At t.J. Maxx may disagree
with you there.

15:27.259 --> 15:28.927
[grunts]

15:32.354 --> 15:34.440
[grunting]

15:34.567 --> 15:36.363
-[grunts]
-huh?

15:36.448 --> 15:37.824
[both grunt]

15:39.414 --> 15:40.956
[panting]

15:41.041 --> 15:43.463
[screaming]

15:44.342 --> 15:45.552
-[man grunts]
-[lois screams]

15:46.723 --> 15:48.893
[grunting]

15:56.371 --> 15:58.041
[grunts]

16:02.303 --> 16:04.891
[both grunting]

16:08.276 --> 16:09.944
-Good day.
-Good day.

16:09.988 --> 16:11.365
Both men:
Good day.

16:11.450 --> 16:14.873
It was them
in the nine-dollar rain bonnets!

16:14.958 --> 16:17.713
Told you these look
like the expensive ones.

16:23.312 --> 16:24.897
[meg gasps]

16:32.794 --> 16:34.629
[groans]

16:35.968 --> 16:37.218
[groans]

16:37.345 --> 16:39.475
Never mess with a mom.

16:39.644 --> 16:41.521
Meg, help me tie up their hands

16:41.606 --> 16:43.358
With these extremely long
cvs receipts.

16:43.444 --> 16:44.905
Why did you save these?

16:44.991 --> 16:46.491
Oh, there's
a carpet-cleaning coupon

16:46.577 --> 16:48.914
On the back
that I'm curious about.

16:51.298 --> 16:53.550
[upbeat,
instrumental rock playing]

16:55.307 --> 16:57.352
I'd like to invite
all the single ladies

16:57.480 --> 16:58.980
To the dance floor!

16:59.107 --> 17:01.236
[screaming]

17:01.322 --> 17:03.408
How about the single fellas?

17:03.535 --> 17:06.039
[cheering, whooping]

17:08.714 --> 17:10.801
Now, some slowly-building
emotional music

17:10.970 --> 17:13.390
For estranged friends
to look at each other

17:13.476 --> 17:16.315
And regret their rift!

17:16.359 --> 17:18.654
[playing slow, gentle music]

17:28.429 --> 17:31.476
Ah. What are we doing?

17:32.313 --> 17:33.522
[microphone feedback squeals]

17:33.608 --> 17:36.196
Hey, I, uh, have a toast.

17:37.618 --> 17:39.161
[clears throat]

17:39.247 --> 17:41.794
You know, sometimes,
against all odds,

17:41.879 --> 17:43.715
Two people find each other

17:43.842 --> 17:46.095
In this crazy place
we call "earth."

17:47.393 --> 17:49.019
Sure, they might have problems,

17:49.104 --> 17:51.150
And they might not always agree
with each other,

17:51.235 --> 17:54.742
And a therapist may even tell
them they shouldn't be friends.

17:55.746 --> 17:57.498
But what I realized is

17:57.626 --> 17:59.502
I don't want a friend
I can get along with.

17:59.631 --> 18:01.257
I can get along with anybody.

18:01.301 --> 18:03.095
[man]
table two hates you, dude!

18:03.139 --> 18:05.768
I want a friend who I can laugh
with because they also noticed

18:05.896 --> 18:07.982
That no one else
is drinking cream soda,

18:08.109 --> 18:10.112
Which means the guy in jeans
brought it from home.

18:10.239 --> 18:11.783
I knew they wouldn't have it!

18:11.910 --> 18:12.995
I want a friend

18:13.081 --> 18:15.124
Who will publicly shame
a mom-and-pop cafe

18:15.243 --> 18:17.337
For having slightly too few
blueberries in their muffin.

18:17.507 --> 18:18.884
[stewie]
call it something else,

18:18.969 --> 18:20.554
'cause it ain't
a blueberry muffin.

18:20.682 --> 18:22.768
Stewie, this is for you.

18:27.699 --> 18:29.993
[playing upbeat rock tune]

18:30.121 --> 18:31.833
<i>♪ stewie, stewie ♪</i>

18:31.960 --> 18:35.507
<i>♪ oh, yeah,
you're my best friend! ♪</i>

18:35.592 --> 18:37.847
He did the work.

18:45.158 --> 18:48.538
Stewie, I'd rather be toxic
and unhealthy together

18:48.624 --> 18:50.419
Than toxic and unhealthy apart.

18:50.547 --> 18:53.092
Me, too, bri.
Let's be best friends again.

18:53.219 --> 18:54.803
What do you say
we hit the photo booth

18:54.890 --> 18:56.684
And take a couple
of funny photos?

18:56.812 --> 18:58.271
I've heard
they have hilarious props.

18:58.398 --> 19:00.693
-No props.
-Yeah, no props, yeah.

19:02.241 --> 19:04.076
<i>[cleveland]
but stewie did use props,</i>

19:04.246 --> 19:05.956
<i> And they had a big fight
about it,</i>

19:06.042 --> 19:07.460
<i> And it took
a whole other wedding</i>

19:07.587 --> 19:08.923
<i> For them to make up again.</i>

19:09.008 --> 19:10.635
<i> I'm cleveland brown,</i>

19:10.720 --> 19:13.683
<i> And I know
my show was better than this.</i>

19:16.860 --> 19:18.905
I can't believe
we made it home safe.

19:18.990 --> 19:21.913
It was so lucky you had
all that stuff in your purse.

19:21.998 --> 19:24.752
Oh, sweetie,
luck had nothing to do with it.

19:24.880 --> 19:27.970
I'm a mom, and moms have
to be prepared for anything.

19:28.055 --> 19:30.349
I really wanted to show you
I could be fun like dad,

19:30.477 --> 19:31.769
But look where that got us.

19:31.896 --> 19:33.231
At the end of the day,

19:33.317 --> 19:35.654
Someone's got
to be the responsible one here.

19:35.739 --> 19:37.157
I guess you're right, mom.

19:37.285 --> 19:39.874
I mean, we all love your
father's water balloon fights,

19:39.959 --> 19:42.504
But someone's got to pick up
all the tiny balloon pieces

19:42.590 --> 19:43.883
From the grass.

19:43.968 --> 19:46.180
That's my role, and it's fine.

19:46.266 --> 19:47.766
Do you think
someday I'll be a boring,

19:47.894 --> 19:49.730
Taken-for-granted wife and mom?

19:49.815 --> 19:52.989
Oh, I think you're well
on your way, sweetheart.

19:57.207 --> 19:59.421
Oh. How was he?

19:59.506 --> 20:01.258
Fine, but let's just say

20:01.344 --> 20:03.972
There's the exact same number
of carrots as when you left.

20:04.099 --> 20:05.853
Well, that sounds about right.

20:06.013 --> 20:07.649
He also said you said

20:07.734 --> 20:10.196
Yogurt-covered pretzels
are a healthy snack.

20:10.281 --> 20:12.160
<i>-[lois sighs]
-[peter] you did say that!</i>

20:12.245 --> 20:15.042
-Compared to cheetos, they are.
-You just said it again!

20:20.390 --> 20:22.225
[clicking, whooshing]

20:22.353 --> 20:24.399
-Here are your waffles.
-Thanks so much.

20:24.526 --> 20:25.776
Yay, that was quick.

20:25.861 --> 20:28.281
[phones whooshing]

20:34.925 --> 20:36.219
Can I grab anything else
for you?

20:36.304 --> 20:38.515
-No, this is great!
-Cheat day!

20:51.382 --> 20:53.426
♪ ♪